---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/04-07/', hk='https://gcnfc.hkust.edu.hk/equipment-other-equipment', uic='https://rrc.uic.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/112/2020/02/Disco_DAD321_Dicing_Saw.pdf#page=1', anff='https://www.anff-sa.com/Instruments/wafer-dicer';
---
<Layout pageTitle="DISCO DAD321 · sealed exterior and passive grid inspection" description="Inspect the stationary enclosure and read two marked locations on a separately authored coordinate poster." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment dad"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/04-07/">← Equipment 04-07</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#dad-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">04-07 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL & DETACHED POSTER / FIRST PASS</span><h2>DISCO DAD321</h2><p>Orbit the sealed DAD321 enclosure. On the separate teaching poster, inspect printed dots and measure the distance between markers A and B. The poster is unrelated to any machine work area or coordinates.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Stationary documentary enclosure</h3><div id="dad-view" aria-label="Orbitable DAD321 bare enclosure with an unpowered beacon and separate teaching display"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-dad-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-dad-view="shell">Exterior face</button><button data-dad-view="display">Detached poster</button><button id="dad-cycle">Switch marker</button></div>
<p id="dad-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal badge on the detached table switches selected poster markers only. The enclosure does not open and its panel has no active controls.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached printed dot grid</h3><canvas id="dad-plot" width="660" height="440" aria-label="A 9-by-7 rectangular display of immutable printed dots. Use column and row fields to select any point without clicking."></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Column X (zero-based)<input id="dad-x" type="number" min="0" max="8" step="1" value="2"/></label><label>Row Y (zero-based)<input id="dad-y" type="number" min="0" max="6" step="1" value="1"/></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="dad-inspect">Inspect marker separation</button><button id="dad-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="dad-status" aria-live="polite">Click a dot or enter a column and row, then inspect the poster.</p><output id="dad-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="dad-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="dad-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: original compact DISCO DAD321 with the legacy vertical cabinet, opaque shell and photographed external signal beacon. The <a href={hk}>HKUST equipment entry</a> gives enclosure dimensions. The <a href={uic}>UIC front photograph, p. 1</a> shows the stack beacon, blankable upper console and lower cabinet proportions. The <a href={anff}>ANFF three-quarter installed photograph</a> shows the angle of the outer hood and stainless ledge. Facing plates and accessories are visually estimated; the opening is replaced by a closed dark opaque facade.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original whole-render of compact DAD321 floor cabinet and separate grid display"/><figcaption>Original whole exterior render, not a photograph. UIC's front view anchors the cabinet silhouette and visible beacon.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original detail of the dark upper console and sealed sloped front hood"/><figcaption>Original close-up compared with the ANFF installation photograph. All controls, guard details, and blanks are decorative only.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Bare cabinet width × depth × height</td><td>500 × 1,050 × 1,455 mm</td><td>Verified in metric GLB, excluding visually estimated optional beacon and detached display.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Poster position A / B</td><td>(10, 23) / (80, 67) mm</td><td>Zero-based [2,1] / [7,5] at the two fixed marker centers in the poster frame.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Marker separation</td><td>√(70² + 44²) mm</td><td>82.680106 mm; out-of-grid selection returns a clear error.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original device acceptance</td><td>Material separation and total area accounting</td><td>Not implemented or run. No tool path, setting, processing, or hardware controls.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>For a printed grid, the dot center is <code>datum + index × pitch</code>. The first center is (−18,12) mm, spacing is 14 mm horizontally and 11 mm vertically, and the logical grid contains 9 × 7 immutable dots. The poster and enclosure use independent frames. Export includes the selected dot, dimensions, fixed marker IDs, vector offset, length and authored provenance. It is not a cut plan, die map, or material simulation.</p>
<p><a href={base+'dad321-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'poster-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/04-07/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.dad{max-width:76rem}.dad .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.dad section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.dad .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.dad .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.dad label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.dad input,.dad select,.dad button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.dad button{cursor:pointer}.dad button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.dad .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.dad #dad-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.dad #dad-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.dad #dad-plot,.dad img{width:100%;height:auto}.dad #dad-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.dad #dad-status.error{color:#a54a34}.dad .scroll{overflow:auto}.dad table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.dad td,.dad th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.dad figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.dad .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
